From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: AVS2: program the picture size in whole 8x8
 blocks

The VE decodes AVS2 in 8x8 minimum coding units and expects the picture
size register to hold the size rounded up to whole units: the vendor
library writes iEncWidth/iEncHeight, (horizontal_size + 7) & ~7 and
(vertical_size + 7) & ~7, there. With the raw size, an 854x480 stream
(width not a multiple of 8) stalls the VE from the first picture and
every job ends in "frame processing timed out".

Round the size up to 8 as the vendor does. The capture buffers are
already aligned to at least 16.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_avs2.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_avs2.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_avs2.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_avs2.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_avs2.c
@@ -433,8 +433,14 @@
 		reg |= VE_DEC_AVS2_SEQ_HDR_BCBR;
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_AVS2_SEQ_HDR, reg);
 
-	reg = VE_DEC_AVS2_PIC_SIZE_WIDTH(seq->horizontal_size) |
-	      VE_DEC_AVS2_PIC_SIZE_HEIGHT(seq->vertical_size);
+	/*
+	 * The picture size in whole 8x8 minimum coding units, as the vendor
+	 * library programs it (its iEncWidth/iEncHeight). An unaligned size,
+	 * such as the 854 pixel width of 480p AVS2, stalls the VE until the
+	 * watchdog fires.
+	 */
+	reg = VE_DEC_AVS2_PIC_SIZE_WIDTH(ALIGN(seq->horizontal_size, 8)) |
+	      VE_DEC_AVS2_PIC_SIZE_HEIGHT(ALIGN(seq->vertical_size, 8));
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_AVS2_PIC_SIZE, reg);
 
 	/* Picture header. */
-- 
